# Introducing ArkType 2.2: Validated functions, type-safe regex, and universal schema interop
created: 2026-03-04, last updated: 2026-03-28, [Read more](https://www.reddit.com/r/typescript/comments/1rkw99x/introducing_arktype_22_validated_functions/)

This update introduces several exciting features, including `type.fn` for functions validated at runtime, type-safe regular expressions through `arkregex`, and bidirectional JSON Schema capabilities with the new `@ark/json-schema` package.
...
the first, the safety that ArkType offers can now encompass the entire function boundary—validating parameters and return values, making them introspectable.
...
Here’s a quick example:
```javascript
len =.fn(" | unknown ":",number")( => s);
len("foo"); // Outputs: 3
len([1, 2]); // Outputs: 2
len(true); // Outputs:aversalError must be string or object (was boolean)
len.expression; // Outputs: "(string | Array) => number"
```
Moreover, you can now combine validators from various ecosystems within a single definition:
```javascript
import { type } from "arktype";
import * as v from "valibot";
import { z } from "zod";
User =({
: "    age v.number    address.object({: z(), city z.string() })
});
```

